* One-character variable indices may omit the dot, and may be written with no
* separator: `s1s2s3` is equivalent to `s1 s2 s3` (reference 1.4).
*
* Each command-line argument arrives as a bracket term, so the pattern unwraps
* one bracket and reverses the three symbols inside it.
$ENTRY Go {
  (s1s2s3) = s3 s2 s1;
}
